00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:15,160
But by adding a billion of them together, I can lift a macroscopic weight.

300
00:21:15,161 --> 00:21:21,660
If the gecko didn't exist, you'd be very, very unlikely that an engineer just sitting

301
00:21:21,661 --> 00:21:27,060
back and thinking about how should I make a novel sticky substance would have ever thought

302
00:21:27,061 --> 00:21:30,040
to make something that looked like a gecko adhesive.

303
00:21:30,041 --> 00:21:35,440
It really tells us that it's so important to save the organisms in our environments,

304
00:21:35,441 --> 00:21:39,200
otherwise the secrets that they have will be lost forever.

305
00:21:39,201 --> 00:21:44,200
While the gecko may be the key to a sticky future, the past is

306
00:21:44,201 --> 00:21:47,200
also alive with sticky secrets.

307
00:21:47,201 --> 00:21:53,200
But there's no mystery about the dangers of this Jurassic stuff.

308
00:21:53,201 --> 00:21:57,200
It's hot.

309
00:21:57,201 --> 00:22:02,200
On 23 acres of prime real estate in Los Angeles sit 100 primeval

310
00:22:02,201 --> 00:22:06,200
pits filled with prehistoric secrets that are trapped within

311
00:22:06,201 --> 00:22:08,500
that are trapped within an ancient sticky stuff.

312
00:22:10,380 --> 00:22:12,220
Known as the La Brea Tar Pits,

313
00:22:12,940 --> 00:22:15,260
these gooey swamps are composed of asphalt,

314
00:22:15,700 --> 00:22:17,060
the lowest grade of crude oil.

315
00:22:19,040 --> 00:22:21,840
Since excavation began in 1906,

316
00:22:22,340 --> 00:22:24,480
more than 1 million bones have been recovered

317
00:22:24,481 --> 00:22:25,500
from the sticky pits,

318
00:22:26,420 --> 00:22:29,860
including mammoths and more than 7,000 dire wolves

319
00:22:29,861 --> 00:22:31,060
and saber-toothed cats.

320
00:22:33,360 --> 00:22:35,900
Centuries ago, asphalt's sticky power

321
00:22:35,901 --> 00:22:38,160
was used to waterproof boats upon the Nile,

322
00:22:39,840 --> 00:22:41,880
as mortar for the great walls of Carthage,

323
00:22:42,340 --> 00:22:44,760
and pavement for roadways to the Acropolis.

324
00:22:47,100 --> 00:22:49,780
All crude oil contains some level of asphalt,

325
00:22:50,320 --> 00:22:52,920
which is removed through a combination of solvents

326
00:22:52,921 --> 00:22:54,480
and distillation during refining.

327
00:22:56,220 --> 00:22:59,680
Today, asphalt manufacturing is a multi-billion-dollar industry.

328
00:23:00,520 --> 00:23:02,880
80% of the product is used to construct roads.

329
00:23:05,900 --> 00:23:08,300
roofing materials consume nearly all the rest.

330
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:14,660
The asphalt used in roofing is sometimes called tar, sometimes called bitumen.

331
00:23:15,360 --> 00:23:19,140
Very rarely is it called asphalt for whatever reason, but it is asphalt.

332
00:23:19,640 --> 00:23:23,500
It has been around for a long, long time,

333
00:23:23,740 --> 00:23:28,040
and it's been around because it is tried and true.

334
00:23:29,540 --> 00:23:33,220
The traditional method of asphalting a roof is known as hot mopping,

335
00:23:33,700 --> 00:23:35,040
with the emphasis on hot.

336
00:23:35,900 --> 00:23:44,980
Hot asphalt and installing built-up roofing systems is a dangerous profession because it is sticky stuff.

337
00:23:45,320 --> 00:23:49,420
And it sticks to you and it burns like crazy.

338
00:23:49,720 --> 00:23:57,260
Even just splashing on your arms, if you look at some roofers, they'll have a lot of little dimples on their arms where it has splashed at some time.

339
00:23:57,580 --> 00:24:01,280
And these guys are skilled. It's very hot. They earn their money.

340
00:24:01,281 --> 00:24:10,040
For this job, asphalt arrives on site as solid 100-pound kegs that are hacked up and heated

341
00:24:10,041 --> 00:24:12,640
into a workable sticky liquid form.

342
00:24:12,641 --> 00:24:20,620
We use a kettle, which is a propane-heated tank of asphalt.

343
00:24:20,621 --> 00:24:24,560
In the morning to start with, it takes probably an hour to get everything all molten and ready

344
00:24:24,561 --> 00:24:25,560
to go.

345
00:24:25,561 --> 00:24:30,960
And there's a thermometer on here so we know when it gets to the 500-450 range so we can

346
00:24:30,961 --> 00:24:32,300
and start pumping it onto the roof.

347
00:24:39,300 --> 00:24:45,140
This roofing job uses the BUR, or built up roofing system,

348
00:24:45,141 --> 00:24:49,880
a precise arrangement of roofing felts and asphalt layers.

349
00:24:49,881 --> 00:24:53,040
The hot asphalt serves as both waterproofing and adhesive

350
00:24:53,041 --> 00:24:56,420
for the roofing felt.

351
00:24:56,421 --> 00:24:59,160
After 45 minutes, the asphalt is cooled,

352
00:24:59,161 --> 00:25:01,800
but hasn't completely hardened.

353
00:25:01,801 --> 00:25:04,020
Actually, it's fairly sticky now.

354
00:25:04,021 --> 00:25:08,120
You can see we'll take this piece of metal and push it in.

355
00:25:08,121 --> 00:25:10,900
And you can see this is cured.

356
00:25:10,901 --> 00:25:12,660
It's cooled down considerably.

357
00:25:12,661 --> 00:25:17,260
As it cools, it becomes a little harder, a little less sticky.

358
00:25:17,261 --> 00:25:21,280
And it melts the felts to the asphalt.

359
00:25:21,281 --> 00:25:23,700
So after 45 minutes, you're about here.

360
00:25:23,701 --> 00:25:25,720
Another 45 minutes, we wouldn't be able to stick this

361
00:25:25,721 --> 00:25:28,020
in here anymore.

362
00:25:28,021 --> 00:25:33,840
When complete, this new roof will last over 20 years.

363
00:25:33,841 --> 00:25:37,800
But asphalt isn't the only sticky stuff with historic roots,

364
00:25:37,801 --> 00:25:42,420
nor is it the only tomb for prehistoric creatures.

365
00:25:42,421 --> 00:25:44,900
Although often thought of as a gemstone,

366
00:25:44,901 --> 00:25:49,260
amber is not a mineral, but a semi-fossilized plant residue

367
00:25:49,261 --> 00:25:52,060
known as rosin.

368
00:25:52,061 --> 00:25:55,880
There's literally thousands of consumer products

369
00:25:55,881 --> 00:25:58,900
that use rosin as a base.

370
00:25:58,901 --> 00:26:03,060
Everything from specialty adhesives found in Band-Aids,

371
00:26:03,061 --> 00:26:06,940
all the way to chewing gum base that we chew on every day,

372
00:26:06,941 --> 00:26:13,140
all the way to citrus beverage drinks, sports drinks.

373
00:26:13,141 --> 00:26:16,420
Rosin's advantage is it melts at a low temperature

374
00:26:16,421 --> 00:26:20,360
and can be blended into gases, liquids, and sprays.

375
00:26:20,361 --> 00:26:23,180
Without rosin, a woman's lipstick, for example,

376
00:26:23,181 --> 00:26:23,881
wouldn't stick.

377
00:26:25,880 --> 00:26:28,960
The finest rosin is found in certain old-growth tree stumps

378
00:26:28,961 --> 00:26:31,400
that have sat for years on the forest floor.

379
00:26:32,980 --> 00:26:34,360
Abandoned by the logging industry,

380
00:26:34,940 --> 00:26:37,500
these stumps continue to possess rosin for decades.

381
00:26:38,620 --> 00:26:41,200
We're looking for the long-leaf pine stumps

382
00:26:41,201 --> 00:26:43,560
that have a lot of rosin and oil in there,

383
00:26:43,820 --> 00:26:46,160
and typically there'll be several hundred pounds

384
00:26:46,161 --> 00:26:48,760
of rosin and oil per ton of stump.

385
00:26:50,860 --> 00:26:54,020
But getting the rosin out of the stump is tricky business.

386
00:26:54,820 --> 00:26:57,240
No one knows that better than the Hercules Corporation,

387
00:26:57,780 --> 00:27:00,520
which has been processing tree rosin for nearly a century.

388
00:27:03,740 --> 00:27:05,780
Here at their Brunswick, Georgia facility,

389
00:27:06,480 --> 00:27:10,280
each stump is placed in the reclaimer that knocks off loose dirt and bark.

390
00:27:11,240 --> 00:27:13,100
Then the real fun begins.

391
00:27:17,360 --> 00:27:21,380
I have control of the reclaimer on and off in this belt here,

392
00:27:21,381 --> 00:27:24,560
which drops the wood in front of the grinder,

393
00:27:24,620 --> 00:27:28,520
and I can cut it on and off depending on the size of the wood

394
00:27:28,521 --> 00:27:30,080
and how much material's coming.

395
00:27:31,080 --> 00:27:34,820
Moisture content in the wood regulates how fast it'll grind a lot of times,

