00:27:34,880 --> 00:27:37,420
and sometimes you have to, you know, throttle back a little bit,

397
00:27:37,520 --> 00:27:41,520
but it's just kind of like just an even float, nice, smooth float.

398
00:27:41,980 --> 00:27:44,720
A lot of energy tearing these things up,

399
00:27:45,200 --> 00:27:47,320
ripping them into about the size of the toothpick,

400
00:27:47,600 --> 00:27:51,300
exposing the wood fibers so they can go on to the next step of our extraction.

